# Study01/ is the repository root as far as the frozen apparatus is concerned:
# `study01/frozen/apparatus.py` pins the sender asset as a path relative to a
# repo root, and `scripts/tests/test_phase1.py` reads this file from that same
# location to prove that finalized hashes survive a real commit and a fresh
# clone. Keep this file here, not only at the Toyotamahime root.

# Keep research documentation and source text stable across Windows and Unix.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Retained capture evidence is binary and must never be EOL-normalized.
# `text=auto` decides by heuristic; evidence integrity must not depend on one.
*.pcap -text

# The K6 Range C comparison targets are the exact bytes the pinned validator
# read and produced, and their SHA-256 values are cited in the expected
# results. They are CRLF as written on the K6 execution host, so no EOL
# heuristic may touch them between hashing and commit. `-diff` as well as
# `-text`: they are hashed byte sequences, not reviewable prose, and a
# line-oriented diff reports every CR as trailing whitespace.
expected/range-c/negative-manifest/** -text -diff
expected/range-c/validator-output/** -text -diff
